      "design": {
        "notes": "Explicit per-eye stereo view synthesis (LeftToRight, non-enlarged). The scene is rendered ONCE (the left eye is the source); the left eye is composed straight to its backbuffer, and the right eye is synthesized from the left via GeometryWarp -> PullpushInpaint and composed to the right backbuffer. Because the graph names both eyes (left_backbuffer/right_backbuffer), render_system renders it once instead of forcing 2-layer multiview. Swap GeometryWarp/PullpushInpaint for a custom Lua backend (see resources/render/passes/xr_custom_warp.lua) to plug in your own synthesis. Enlarged-source (IncreaseFov/ReduceFov) lands with the XrSynthesisPlan camera math.",
        "status": "active"
      },
